From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] bridge: expose minimal part-state getters

Read-only accessors for state the bridge publishes; each is added only
because no existing public API exposes the value (checked against
HEAD): Ball::GetID (m_id private, no accessor), Flipper::GetHitFlipper
(get_AngleEOS is commented out; angle lives on the hit object),
Gate::GetHitGate, Plunger::GetHitPlunger, Spinner::GetHitSpinner
(mover state lives on the hit objects), Bumper::GetBumperHitCircle/
GetSkirtRotX/GetSkirtRotY (ring/skirt fields private, script-only),
HitTarget::GetMoveAnimationOffset, Trigger::GetAnimHeightOffset,
Primitive::GetCurrentFrame (animation state, no accessors). Heavier
alternatives (script IDispatch, friend declarations) were avoided.

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

diff --git a/src/parts/ball.h b/src/parts/ball.h
index a44f90eb0..45d306030 100644
--- a/src/parts/ball.h
+++ b/src/parts/ball.h
@@ -230,6 +230,9 @@ private:
    static unsigned int GetNextBallID();
 
    const unsigned int m_id; // unique ID for each ball
